  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "Because the bias, RMSE, correlation and model ranking must be computed only on cells all fields share, using one mask over the models and WOA23 and keeping WOA23's land-sea mask only for this WOA23 comparison.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Put all three `tos` climatologies and WOA23 on the WOA23 1° grid, build one mask over all of them with `build_comparison_mask`, and apply it with `.where(mask)` to every field before any bias, RMSE or correlation; never score or rank models on per-model pairwise masks.",
        "`ocean_only=True` (the default) is right here because WOA23 is the reference; report the cell counts the mask records next to the metrics — a mask much smaller than the individual fields means the products disagree about where the ocean is."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "Because each model's global mean must be area-weighted over its native ocean grid using areacello, not taken as an unweighted cell average.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Native-grid global means are Σ tos·areacello / Σ areacello over valid ocean cells (never an unweighted `mean()` over y,x); use `compute_basic_stat` with `op='area_weighted_mean'`, with the weights masked to the same cells as the valid data.",
        "`compute_difference_metrics` weights by area by default; `analyze_correlation` needs `weighting='area'`. Report the shared-sample means it returns (`mean_data`, `mean_reference`); a model's own-grid global mean and its model-minus-WOA23 bias on the shared mask are different quantities."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-grid-labels.md",
      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "Because CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are gn curvilinear native grids whereas GFDL-ESM4 is gr regridded, which affects masks and which operations are exact.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 `tos` sits on archive grid `gr` (remapped to 1°, conserve_order1), so its \"native\" numbers are on the regridded grid with a regridded land–sea mask.",
        "Resolution differs by about 2.5 between CESM2 (100 km) and MPI (250 km); features narrower than the coarse grid are not comparable in amplitude when describing the bias structure."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "Because areacello is the tracer-cell horizontal area needed as the weight for each model's native ocean-grid global mean.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Take the area weight for each native-grid mean from that model's own `areacello` (`load_areas` records `attrs['area_source']`).",
        "Total ocean area differs between models by a per cent or so because the coastline is resolved differently; state the area each mean was taken over rather than rescaling one model to another."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-tos-bulk-top-cell",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-tos-bulk-top-cell.md",
      "sha256": "4acdeba0f49784d4435dbc4eed34ca9777254313daa951641759fa02df24cf64",
      "reason": "Because tos is top-cell bulk potential temperature, not a skin SST, so the comparison with WOA23 0 m temperature must be stated in those terms.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`tos` is the bulk temperature of the top model cell including under sea ice (near −1.8 °C), not a skin value, so its global mean contains near-freezing polar values; if the observational product masks sea ice, the masks must be made consistent first.",
        "Top-cell thickness differs (CESM2 0–10 m, GFDL-ESM4 0–2 m, MPI-ESM1-2-LR 0–12 m), so part of any inter-model mean difference is definitional, not error."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "Because CMIP6 land and below-sea-floor cells are marked with 1e20 and must be CF-masked before sums or means, or they silently corrupt global means and biases.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "xarray decodes the 1e20 fill to NaN; build each field's valid mask from the field itself (masks differ between variables of one model) and mask the weights to those cells, so land stays missing instead of contributing 0.",
        "A value near 1e20 (or 9.97e36) in any output is an unmasked fill value, not a result."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-experiments-historical-ssp245",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-experiments-historical-ssp245.md",
      "sha256": "be5515ae7b8c8826c4e329bddcd5cbadc8e3e000292b7f6e83e1537af36a990c",
      "reason": "Because the historical simulations are free-running coupled runs whose years are not synchronised with observed years, so the 1971-2000 climatological bias includes internal variability as well as forced model bias.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "These are coupled historical runs: statistics over the 1971–2000 window are comparable, individual years and event timing are not; with one member per model, forced change cannot be separated from internal variability, so the bias and ranking results must carry that caveat."
      ]
    }
